                    {
                        "sense_id": "48944cb0-e3a8-3052-a38f-3a9406942435",
                        "entry_id": "65d75d46-5a83-38e3-af8e-1e6e83b0b4a6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to fool (someone)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d65cee2-0323-4836-9449-d36fe66ba871",
                                "sense_id": "48944cb0-e3a8-3052-a38f-3a9406942435",
                                "text": "Зинаи́да то́тчас же догада́лась, что я в неё влюби́лся, да я и не ду́мал скрыва́ться; она́ потеша́лась мое́й стра́стью, дура́чила, балова́ла и му́чила меня́.",
                                "translation": "Zinaïda guessed at once that I was in love with her, and indeed I never even thought of concealing it. She amused herself with my passion, made a fool of me, petted and tormented me.",
                                "english": "Zinaïda guessed at once that I was in love with her, and indeed I never even thought of concealing it. She amused herself with my passion, made a fool of me, petted and tormented me."
                            }
                        ]
